    "body": "- [x] I have searched open and closed issues for duplicates\r\n- [x] I am submitting a bug report for existing functionality that does not work as intended\r\n- [x] I have read https://github.com/signalapp/Signal-Android/wiki/Submitting-useful-bug-reports\r\n- [x] This isn't a feature request or a discussion topic\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------\r\n\r\n### Bug description\r\nRandom \"Locked Message\" notifications that supposedly just say: \"Contact XYZ is on Signal!\";\r\nThe thing is... they're not! On multiple occasions, I've called these people and they've never even heard about the app.\r\nFor most of my contacts, especially friends and family, I'm their \"go-to IT person\", so I'm pretty darn sure they would ask me if it's OK or safe to move from WhatsApp/Telegram/Messenger/whatever to Signal since they've done exactly that previously on other occasions. However, I see complete non-technical people pop up (and I'll say it again, I've confirmed with them and they've never heard about Signal) in my notifications.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n- can't really reproduce it myself... it just happens randomly, it seems?\r\n\r\n**Actual result:** Random message about my contacts supposedly joining Signal (and they haven't).\r\n**Expected result:** Only get the notification if they indeed have already joined Signal.\r\n\r\n### Screenshots\r\nI don't have the notification right now, but you can see my chat list...\r\n*[redacted]*\r\n\r\n### Device info\r\n**Device:** One+ 6T\r\n**Android version:** 10 (Oxygen 10.3.9)\r\n**Signal version:** 5.8.3\r\n\r\n### Link to debug log\r\nhttps://debuglogs.org/480377deea5a18f44c54c9efb71c9931a067b6e277d763121c925a26c01c5c97\r\n",
